== YAML Turned 25 This Year!

* YAML implementations in over %50 languages%
  * Ada, C, C++, C#, CFML, Clojure, Common Lisp, Crystal, D, Dart, Delphi,
    Dyalog APL, Elixir, Erlang, F#, Fortran, ^Go^, Groovy, Haskell, Haxe, Java,
    JavaScript, Julia, Kotlin, Lua, ML, MoonBit, Nim, Objective-C, OCaml, Octave,
    Perl, PHP, PowerShell, PureScript, Python, R, Racket, Raku, Ruby, Rust,
    Scala, Scheme, Shell, Swift, Tcl, TypeScript, Typst, V, Vala, Vim, Zig
  * https://yaml.org/libraries/

* Multiple implementations in most languages
  * 5 implementations in ^Go^ :-)

* YAML is used almost everywhere you look
  * Kubernetes, Docker, Ansible, CI
  * General configuration
  * Nearly ^80% of active GitHub repos^ have a YAML file

----
== YAML has some Problems

* The YAML spec is huge
  * But is it `impossible to change`?
  * Would need to be implemented in every language :\

* Many implementations are still YAML 1.1 (@2005@)
  * YAML 1.2 dates to @2009@ (updated in @2021@)

* No two YAML implementations are fully compatible :-(

----
== The YAML Family Tree

* Most top %YAMLs are descended from PyYAML% (2005)
  * %NOT% from the spec :\

* I call these ^The YAML Family^

* %PyYAML%     - 2005 - Kirill Simonov   - The OG YAML
* `libyaml`    - 2006 - Kirill Simonov   - Port of PyYAML
  * YAML shared library for many languages:
      Ruby, Python, Perl, PHP, Lua, R
* `snakeyaml`  - 2009 - Andrey Somov     - Port of PyYAML
* ^go-yaml    - 2014 - Gustavo Niemeyer - Port of libyaml^
* `serde-yaml` - 2016 - David Tolnay     - Port of libyaml (Rust)

* Many ported bugs:
  * https://play.yaml.com/?show=gdhflLnJPpxHUrsS#Zm9vOiB7OiBiYXJ9

