----
== What if YAML were Fully Programmable?

* Introducing YAMLScript (YS)

* Lets any YAML data be code

* https://yamlscript.org

----
== Python Data as Config

* %You _could_ use Python code as a config language…%

# A Python config program, using only data syntax:

{
    "service": "yaml-api",
    "host": "127.0.0.1",
    "port": 8080,
    "debug": False,
    "workers": 4,
    "allowed_origins": ["https://example.com"],
}

* Show as JSON
$ python -c 'import json;print(json.dumps(eval(open("config-1.py").read())))' | jq .

----
== YAMLScript == Dynamic Python as Config

# Same thing using code to calculate some data values:

{
    "service": "yaml-api",
    "host": ".".join(["127", "0", "0", "1"]),
    "port": 8000 + 80,
    "debug": 1 > 2,
    "workers": 2 * 2,
    "allowed_origins": ["https://example.com"],
}

$ python -c 'import json;print(json.dumps(eval(open("config-1.py").read())))' | jq .

----
== Dynamic YAML as Config

# Same thing as Python, but the code is YAML:

    !ys-0:
    service: yaml-api
    host:: +[127 0 0 1].join('.')
    port:: 8000 + 80
    debug:: 1 > 2
    workers:: 2 * 2
    allowed_origins: [https://example.com]

$ ys -J sample.yaml

* `::` means value is a code expression

