----
== What if there was a @100% Compatible YAML Library@ for every language?

* Full featured
* Same in every language
  * Same API
  * Same features
  * Same bugs
  * Same fixes

----
== Introducing YAMLStar

* https://yamlstar.org
  * A YAML framework for 32 programming languages (so far!)

* YAMLStar works the same in every language
  * Same API, same features, same bugs, same fixes

* YAMLStar ALSO has a ^Plugin System^!
  * Same plugins for all languages
  * ^Most plugins are shared with go-yaml!!^

* Has a CLI called "yaml", very similar to the "go-yaml" CLI
  $ go-yaml -J <<<'a: [ok, 1, 2.3, true, null]'
  $ yaml    -J <<<'a: [ok, 1, 2.3, true, null]'

----
== YAMLStar -> New YAML Spec!

* YAML 1.2 dates to 2009
  * Many YAMLs are still at 1.1

* YAMLStar has plugins
  * Plugins let us try new things
  * go-yaml has many of the same plugins!

* ^Popular new ideas become part of the next spec^
  * Implementations in every language
  * Before the spec is published!
  * YAMLStar and %go-yaml plugins are the key to YAML 1.3!%

* YAMLStar is how we get to %YAML 1.3% (or 2.0)!
  * Working ^implementations in every language^ *before* release!
  * Plugins let us ^experiment with new ideas^ in YAML 1.2…
    before deciding what goes into the next YAML spec!

+* %Back to go-yaml Plugins!%

----
== What if YAML supported tab indentation?

$ cat tabs.yaml
$ sed 's/\t/=>/g' tabs.yaml  # Prove really tabs!

* ^Works in both YAMLStar and go-yaml!^
$ yaml    -J --plugin=tab-indent tabs.yaml
$ go-yaml -J --plugin=tab-indent tabs.yaml

* And in Go code, of course:
$ vim tabs.go
$ go run tabs.go

----
== What if you could write ^go-yaml plugins in YS^?

* %YS is Go%. Should be easy!

* We can swap out %the entire Parser% for go-yaml
  * With the `YAML-Parser` plugin API

* ^There is already 7 current parser plugins:^
  go-yaml       - Native Go parser (default for go-yaml & YAMLStar)
  reference     - YAML reference grammar parser
  snakeyaml     - Java's SnakeYAML Engine parser
  rapidyaml     - C++ RapidYAML parser
  json-comments - YAML parser supporting C-style comments
  %toml          - Parse TOML to YAML events%
  ^csv           - Parse CSV/TSV to YAML events^

----
== yamlstar-plugin-parser-csv

* I wrote a ^CSV/TSV^ parser plugin for go-yaml
  * %In YAMLScript!%

* https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yamlstar/yamlstar-plugin-parser-csv/refs/heads/main/src/csv_parser/core.ys

* A CSV file:
$ cat data.csv

* Need to build the go-yaml CLI with it:
$ make -C repos/go-yaml cli PLUGIN-PACKAGE=github.com/yamlstar/yamlstar-plugin-parser-csv/goyaml@v0.1.0

* Try it out:
$ go-yaml -J --plugin=yaml-parser=csv data.csv

* Parses CSV to go-yaml Event structs:
$ go-yaml -e --plugin=yaml-parser=csv data.csv

----
== YAML Plugin APIs

* ^Alias-Data^      - Powerful aliasing
* Allowed-Bugs    - Choose which fixed bugs to retain
* Comment-Model   - Better comment loading
* ^Error-Format^    - Custom error formatting
* ^Function-Tag^    - Define your own function calls: `!import vars: vars.yaml`
* L10N-Keys       - YAML keys in French or Chinese
* ^Loader-Limits^   - Custom resource limits
* Merge-Key       - Custom `<<` merge key behavior
* Multi-Tag       - Multiple tags `!!foo;bar`
* Stream-Tag      - `!!yaml:helm.sh/v4`
* String-Expand   - Alias/Reference/Variable/Expression Interpolation
* ^Tab-Indent^      - Use tabs for YAML indentation
* YAML-Format     - Completely custom YAML formatting
* ^YAML-Parser^     - Use an alternate YAML parser
* %YAML-Rules%      - Use `oui` and `non` for `true` and `false`
* YAML-Schema     - Schema validation and association

+* That's all I have for you today…

